# mimeapps.list — generated by hyprsetup
#
# DEFAULT APPLICATIONS COME FROM HERE. The single source for which app opens
# which file type is the DEFAULT_APP_ROLES / DEFAULT_APP_COMPONENT_ROLES tables
# in python/hyprsetup/render.py; each role in the table looks at the "desktop"
# field of the component in config/components.json. So FILEMANAGER="dolphin"
# means dolphin's .desktop entry feeds both the file manager keybinding and
# the inode/directory association here — the two are never fed separately.
#
# To change it by hand, do not edit this file (it is regenerated on every
# install); instead of ~/.config/mimeapps.list use your desktop's own "Default
# Applications" screen, or change TERMINAL / FILEMANAGER / BROWSER in
# settings.conf and run './install.sh --reapply'.
#
# [Default Applications] is the user's choice and takes precedence over the
# system's /usr/share/applications/mimeinfo.cache guesses;
# [Added Associations] only feeds the "Open with" list and does not set the
# default — so both are written with the same associations.

